  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ce4091efa6b73194680553dd3dac51da, type: 3}
  m_Name: Garage_Storage
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  sequence:
  - background: {fileID: 0}
    clearBackground: 0
    speakerName: Ryuuji
    dialogue:
    - (Just a general storage room full of old junk.)
    - (There's a few mementos in there too.)
    - (I think the oldest thing in there might be Inko-chan's birdcage.)
    - (Ever since she passed away, it's been collecting dust.)
    - (I asked Yasuko if she wanted to take it with her, but she seemed content with
      leaving it with my daughters.)
    - (They really loved playing with Inko-chan, so they were distraught when they
      received the news.)
    - (Well... Haruko and Mitsuko were, at least. Katsuko and Inko-chan never got
      along. Somehow, when I left them alone, they were both covered in bites.)
    - (When Inko-chan passed, Katsuko cried, but she got over it quickly. Then she
      said something insensitive that made Haruko cry even more than she already
      was, and they wouldn't speak to each other for the rest of the week.)
    - (Haruko was the one that played with Inko-chan the most. Little girls can be
      so cruel. Of course, now that they're older, it's water under the bridge.)
    - (Yasuko's got a new pet now. A healthy cat named Inko-sama. Inko-chan's passing
      upset her a lot too, even more than it upset my daughters, but I think she's
      over that now.)
    - (When I have nothing to do, I'd clean the dust off that cage. It's basically
      good as new now, though part of me would feel a little uneasy at the lack of
      bird poop staining the metal.)
